carry.nobody = You are not carrying anyone.
carry.picked_up = You lift {name} onto your shoulders.
carry.put_down = You set {name} back down.
carry.already = {name} is already being carried.
carry.hint = Crouch and click a block to put them down. If that does not work, use /simtale putdown.
carry.stackFull = You can only carry {count} at a time.
carry.stacked = {name} climbs up onto the ones you are already carrying.

# Lines spoken by NPCs outside the interaction panel: leaving for work, coming back,
# giving up on a conversation, and the spouse handing the baby over. Moved out of
# general.lang, which is for system messages — these are a character speaking.
tick.job.depart.1 = {name}: I'm leaving now! I'll be back as soon as I finish.
tick.job.depart.2 = {name}: I'm off! I'll be back later.
tick.job.depart.3 = {name}: Off to work! I'll finish up shortly.
tick.job.complete.1 = {name}: I finished my {job_name} work and came back!
tick.job.complete.2 = {name}: Phew, done with the {job_name} work. I'm back!
tick.job.complete.3 = {name}: Mission accomplished! The {job_name} job is complete.
tick.chat.timeout.1 = {name}: Hmm, I think you're busy. Let's talk later!
tick.chat.timeout.2 = {name}: You seem distracted... we can talk later!
tick.chat.timeout.3 = {name}: I see you're not in a chatting mood today. Bye!
baby.custody.spouse_reject = <{spouse}> Now it's your turn to take care of {name} for a while.

# Lines for the baby you are carrying. They live here rather than in general.lang
# because they are a character speaking; general.lang is for system messages.
baby.babble.1 = The baby in your arms: goo... goo-goo... gaga!
baby.babble.2 = The baby giggles and grabs your finger.
baby.babble.3 = The baby: aaaaa-booo!
baby.babble.4 = The baby yawns very slowly and settles in.
baby.babble.5 = The baby blows a spit bubble and seems very pleased with it.
baby.babble.6 = The baby: da-da? da-da!
baby.babble.7 = The baby stares at you, solemnly, for an uncomfortable while. Then smiles.
baby.babble.8 = The baby whimpers softly and stops the moment you rock them a little.

friendly.greeting.1 = {name} smiles: Hello! Good to see you around today.
friendly.greeting.2 = {name} waves: Hey! How are things?
friendly.greeting.3 = {name}: Hey there! Any news in Orbis?
friendly.greeting.4 = {name} smiles friendly: Hi! I'm glad you came to talk.
friendly.greeting.5 = {name}: Hello! I was just wondering when we'd see each other again.
greedy.greeting.1 = {name} rubs their hands: Do you have any extra ore or items for me today?
greedy.greeting.2 = {name} looks at your backpack: Hmm, so many shiny things in there... don't want to share?
greedy.greeting.3 = {name} winks: Hello! Did you come to bring me gifts or just to chit-chat?
paranoid.greeting.1 = {name} looks around sweating cold: Shh! Did you hear that?...
paranoid.greeting.2 = {name} whispers nervously: They are watching us... act naturally!
paranoid.greeting.3 = {name} pulls you aside: Did you see that bush move? I'm sure it was a Trork spy.
lazy.greeting.1 = {name} yawns: Oh, hi... Wake me up when dinner is ready.
lazy.greeting.2 = {name} stretches: Hi... So sleepy. Did you say something important?
lazy.greeting.3 = {name} sighs lazily: Hi. If it's about work, tell them I'm not here.
context.bleeding = {name} widens their eyes: Oh my god, you're bleeding! Do you need help?!
context.night = {name} whispers: It's dangerous to walk around here at night... Be careful.
context.insulted.recent = {name} crosses their arms: What do you want? Haven't you insulted me enough today?
context.insulted.other = {name} glares at you: I heard what you did to {otherName}. You better walk the line.
context.attacked.recent = {name} backs away in fear: Stay away from me! You attacked me!
context.attacked.other = {name} glares at you with suspicion: I heard you attacked {otherName}... Stay away from me!
context.missed = {name} widens their eyes: Wow, I haven't seen you in days! Where were you?!
funny.angry.1 = {name}: ...was that supposed to be funny?
funny.angry.2 = {name} sighs: I'm not in the mood for jokes today.
funny.angry.3 = {name} stares at you seriously: Please spare me from your jokes right now.
funny.angry.4 = {name} shakes their head: Unfunny. Very unfunny.
funny.angry.5 = {name} crosses their arms: I have real problems here and you come to me with jokes?
funny.trait.1 = {name}: HAHAHA! Good one! You have a knack for comedy.
funny.trait.2 = {name} laughs loudly: Oh my god, that was genius! I'll have to tell the others.
funny.trait.3 = {name} cries laughing: Oh no, stop! My stomach hurts from laughing so much! Hahaha!
funny.trait.4 = {name} gives you a friendly pat on the shoulder: Hahaha, you're quite a character! Loved it!
funny.trait.5 = {name} laughs out loud: Very good! I knew you were funny, but that topped it.
funny.normal.1 = You told a joke! {name} laughed a lot.
funny.normal.2 = {name} gives a light chuckle: Heh, that was a good one. Thanks for the smile.
funny.normal.3 = {name} smiles with humor: Nice try! I hadn't heard that one.
funny.normal.4 = You shared a funny joke and {name} gave a beautiful smile.
funny.normal.5 = {name} lets out a muffled laugh: Hahaha, ok, that was kinda cute.
romantic.reject.1 = {name}: Dude... what? Go away.
romantic.reject.2 = {name} looks at you with disdain: Less, way less. We don't have that intimacy.
romantic.reject.3 = {name} takes a step back: Please keep those comments to yourself.
romantic.reject.4 = {name} crosses their arms rolling their eyes: I think you got the wrong person. Leave me alone.
romantic.reject.5 = {name} says coldly: What a cheap pickup line. I don't fall for that.
romantic.shy.1 = {name} blushes and looks away: T-thank you... you're not bad yourself.
romantic.shy.2 = {name} stammers red: Ah... I-I... thank you. You take me by surprise like that.
romantic.shy.3 = {name} covers their shy face: P-stop looking at me like that, it's making me awkward!
romantic.shy.4 = {name} gives an embarrassed smile: You always say these things so suddenly... silly.
romantic.shy.5 = {name} bites their lip in shame: Ah... thank you for the compliment. I'm happy.
romantic.normal.1 = {name}: Heh... keep talking. I'm enjoying listening.
romantic.normal.2 = {name} winks: Really? Who knows, if you insist a little more...
romantic.normal.3 = {name} smirks: Well look at that, a charmer around here. Interesting.
romantic.normal.4 = {name} smiles confidently: I know I'm amazing, but it's always good to hear it from you.
romantic.normal.5 = {name} gives a charming smile: You really know how to charm someone, don't you?
kiss.success.1 = {name} closes their eyes and returns the kiss tenderly.
kiss.success.2 = {name} smiles mid-kiss, heart racing.
kiss.success.3 = {name} leans in closer, lost in the moment.
kiss.reject = {name} turns their face away: We're not quite that close yet...
young.chat.village_child.1 = {name} stares up at you: You're HUGE. Were you ever little?
young.chat.village_child.2 = {name}: My mum said not to talk to strangers. But you look alright.
young.chat.village_child.3 = {name} points at the sky: Look at that bird! Does it live up there?
young.chat.village_child.4 = {name}: I found a rock today. It's my best rock.
young.chat.village_child.5 = {name} runs around you twice and stops, out of breath: Hi!
young.chat.village_child.6 = {name}: Did you know if you spin really fast you get dizzy? I tried it already.
young.chat.village_child.7 = {name} sniffs a flower and sneezes: Ow! That one was stronger than I expected.
young.chat.village_child.8 = {name} looks down at your shoes: Yours are huge! I bet my whole foot could fit inside one of them.
young.chat.village_child.9 = {name}: I can count to a hundred without messing up! Want to see? One, two, three...
young.chat.village_child.10 = {name} tugs your sleeve: Come on, come on! There's a huge frog by the well, I saw it!
young.chat.village_child.11 = {name} shows off a scraped knee proudly: I fell out of the tree, but I almost grabbed the branch!
young.chat.village_child.12 = {name}: If I stay really still, the birds come right up close. You be quiet too!

young.chat.own_child.1 = {name} tugs your sleeve: {parent}, look at that bird! It's looking at me!
young.chat.own_child.2 = {name}: When I grow up I'm going to be just like you. But taller.
young.chat.own_child.3 = {name} holds up two muddy hands: Look what I found! It's a bug. I'm going to name it.
young.chat.own_child.4 = {name}: Will you be back before dark? I don't like it when it's dark and you're not here.
young.chat.own_child.5 = {name} hugs your leg and says nothing for a little while.
young.chat.own_child.6 = {name}: {parent}, can I maybe stay up a little later today? Just a bit?
young.chat.own_child.7 = {name} draws something on the ground with a stick: Look, that's me. And that's you, {parent}.
young.chat.own_child.8 = {name} tugs your hand: {parent}, can you stay a little longer? Just a little bit more.
young.chat.own_child.9 = {name}: I told my friends you're the strongest one in the village. I hope that's true.
young.chat.own_child.10 = {name} hides something behind their back: I made this for you, {parent}. It's not pretty, but it's yours.
young.chat.own_child.11 = {name}: {parent}, are you scared of anything? Because I am, and I wanted to know if it goes away when you grow up.
young.chat.own_child.12 = {name}, yawning but fighting it: I'm not sleepy, {parent}. I swear. — and dozes off standing up.

young.chat.own_teen.1 = {name} shrugs: Hey. I'm fine, you can stop asking.
young.chat.own_teen.2 = {name}: I can handle myself, you know. I'm not a kid.
young.chat.own_teen.3 = {name} looks away: ...I saw you across the village today. I didn't say anything, there were people.
young.chat.own_teen.4 = {name}: This place is too small. One day I want to see what's on the other side.
young.chat.own_teen.5 = {name} almost smiles: Fine. It was nice having you around today. Don't tell anyone.
young.chat.own_teen.6 = {name}: Fine, I'll admit it. It was good seeing you today. I'm not saying it again, though.
young.chat.own_teen.7 = {name} leans on the wall, more serious than usual: Sometimes I wish I could just... I don't know. Be little again.
young.chat.own_teen.8 = {name}: No, I don't want to talk about "feelings." I just came to say hi.
young.chat.own_teen.9 = {name} nudges the ground with their foot: I didn't come to talk about anything important. Just... was around.
young.chat.own_teen.10 = {name}: Sometimes I hear you two talking at night. It's weird thinking that one day I'll be the one saying those things.
young.chat.own_teen.11 = {name} crosses their arms, but sticks around anyway: I didn't come looking for you. It was a coincidence.
young.chat.own_teen.12 = {name}: Did you know some people my age have already left the village? I wouldn't leave, just... think about it sometimes.

young.chat.own_adult.1 = {name} greets you with a nod: All good here. You looking after yourself?
young.chat.own_adult.2 = {name}: Remember when I was small and thought that hill was the end of the world?
young.chat.own_adult.3 = {name} smiles: I've started talking like you. Noticed it the other day and it terrified me.
young.chat.own_adult.4 = {name}: If you ever need anything, just say. I mean it.
young.chat.own_adult.5 = {name}: I'm building my life here. It worked out, in the end.
young.chat.own_adult.6 = {name}: Glad you showed up. I was going to look for you later anyway.
young.chat.own_adult.7 = {name} looks around: The village has grown so much since I was little. It's strange, in a good way.
young.chat.own_adult.8 = {name}: You know I still remember every story you used to tell me? I kept all of them.
young.chat.own_adult.9 = {name} looks at their own hands: Funny, I have your hands. Only noticed the other day.
young.chat.own_adult.10 = {name}: If I ever have a kid, I hope I manage half of what you did for me.
young.chat.own_adult.11 = {name} laughs to themselves: I was thinking about some silly thing I used to do as a kid. Do you remember?
young.chat.own_adult.12 = {name}: I don't know if I've ever said this, but... thanks. For everything, really.

young.joke.village_child.1 = {name} bursts out laughing and can't stop. It wasn't even that funny.
young.joke.village_child.2 = {name} laughs and immediately tries to tell it back to you, ruining the ending.
young.joke.village_child.3 = {name} wheezes: I'm telling my mum that one!
young.joke.village_child.4 = {name} laughs so hard they get hiccups.
young.joke.village_child.5 = {name}: I don't get it. — pause — Oh! I GET IT! — and laughs alone.
young.joke.village_child.6 = {name} points at you laughing: Say it again! Say it again!
young.joke.village_child.7 = {name} tries to hold back the laugh and completely fails, laughing with their nose running.
young.joke.village_child.8 = {name} laughs so loud it startles a bird nearby.
young.joke.village_child.9 = {name}: Wait, let me go try that on my friends! — runs off before you can respond.
young.joke.village_child.10 = {name} points at their own belly: It hurts from laughing so much! But keep going, keep going!
young.joke.village_child.11 = {name} laughs while covering their mouth with both hands, eyes nearly shut from laughing so hard.
young.joke.village_child.12 = {name}: That was the funniest thing I've ever heard IN MY WHOLE LIFE. — which has lasted about six years.

young.joke.own_child.1 = {name} howls with laughter: {parent}, tell it again! TELL IT AGAIN!
young.joke.own_child.2 = {name} laughs and sits down in the grass from laughing.
young.joke.own_child.3 = {name}: You're the funniest one in the whole village. I asked everyone already.
young.joke.own_child.4 = {name} quietly repeats the joke to themselves so they won't forget it.
young.joke.own_child.5 = {name} laughs, then goes serious. Wait. Is that true?
young.joke.own_child.6 = {name} rolls on the ground laughing: {parent}, stop, stop, I can't take it anymore!
young.joke.own_child.7 = {name}: I'm going to remember that joke for the rest of my life, {parent}.
young.joke.own_child.8 = {name}: {parent}, you should tell jokes to everyone in the village. They don't know what they're missing.
young.joke.own_child.9 = {name} laughs so hard they run out of breath, and still tries to squeeze out a bit more laughing.
young.joke.own_child.10 = {name} hugs you in the middle of laughing, for no reason other than being happy.
young.joke.own_child.11 = {name}: Can I tell this one to my teacher tomorrow? She never laughs at anything.
young.joke.own_child.12 = {name} wipes away a tear from laughing: {parent}, stop, my belly already hurts!

young.joke.own_teen.1 = {name} holds back a laugh: That joke's ancient. — the corner of their mouth gives it away.
young.joke.own_teen.2 = {name}: Not funny. — laughs three seconds later, against their will.
young.joke.own_teen.3 = {name} rolls their eyes and smiles at the same time, which takes some effort.
young.joke.own_teen.4 = {name}: If you tell that one near my friends I'm leaving the village.
young.joke.own_teen.5 = {name} properly laughs, and seems annoyed at themselves about it.
young.joke.own_teen.6 = {name} bites their lip trying not to laugh and fails miserably.
young.joke.own_teen.7 = {name}: Okay, that was... — stops, breathes — okay, that was actually funny. Just this once.
young.joke.own_teen.8 = {name} turns their face away laughing, pretending it was a sneeze.
young.joke.own_teen.9 = {name}: Okay, I'm keeping that one. To use later and pretend I made it up.
young.joke.own_teen.10 = {name} lets out a short laugh and immediately goes quiet, like they'd given themselves away.
young.joke.own_teen.11 = {name}: I didn't laugh. You saw wrong. — still smiling.
young.joke.own_teen.12 = {name} shakes their head, smiling despite themselves: You're ridiculous. That's great.

young.joke.own_adult.1 = {name} laughs: That's the same joke from when I was six. Still bad.
young.joke.own_adult.2 = {name}: I tell that one around, you know. And I say I made it up.
young.joke.own_adult.3 = {name} shakes their head, smiling: You really don't change.
young.joke.own_adult.4 = {name} laughs, then goes quiet for a moment. Good memory.
young.joke.own_adult.5 = {name}: Saving that one for my own kids some day.
young.joke.own_adult.6 = {name} really laughs: You've still got it, huh.
young.joke.own_adult.7 = {name}: Glad someone around here is still funny. I needed that.
young.joke.own_adult.8 = {name}: That's exactly the kind of joke I tell my friends, you know?
young.joke.own_adult.9 = {name} laughs for real, from deep in the chest: It's been a while since I laughed like that.
young.joke.own_adult.10 = {name}: I have to admit, your sense of humor was always good. Even when I pretended it wasn't.
young.joke.own_adult.11 = {name} shakes their head laughing: You're never going to stop trying to make me laugh, are you?
young.joke.own_adult.12 = {name}: Thank you for that. Really. Needed a laugh today.

scold.child.1 = {name} looks at the floor and says nothing. Their lip is trembling.
scold.child.2 = {name} looks down and scuffs the floor with their foot, saying nothing.
scold.child.3 = {name} shrinks down and goes quiet, eyes welling up.
scold.child_excessive.1 = {name} bursts into tears: You're always angry at me! I didn't even do anything!
scold.child_excessive.2 = {name} sobs, hiding their face: Why do you only ever yell at me?!
scold.child_excessive.3 = {name} chokes up: I really try to be good, I swear! Please stop fighting with me!
scold.teen.1 = {name} rolls their eyes: Fine. Whatever you say.
scold.teen.2 = {name} crosses their arms: Okay, got it, you can stop now.
scold.teen.3 = {name} lets out an exaggerated sigh: Ugh, fine, I get it.
scold.teen_excessive.1 = {name} shouts back: You never listen! I'm not a kid anymore! — and storms off.
scold.teen_excessive.2 = {name} stomps a foot: You always overreact! I'm not a little kid! — and turns away.
scold.teen_excessive.3 = {name} raises their voice: I'm done with this! Stop treating me like a baby! — and storms out.
scold.adult.1 = {name} sighs: Alright, alright. You're still my parent, after all.
scold.adult.2 = {name} shakes their head: Fine, fine. Noted.
scold.adult.3 = {name} shrugs: Alright, I'm listening.
scold.adult_excessive.1 = {name} raises an eyebrow: I'm a grown adult. Maybe ease off a little.
scold.adult_excessive.2 = {name} crosses their arms: I'm not a kid who needs this every day.
scold.adult_excessive.3 = {name} takes a breath: Rough day for you, huh. Try to relax a bit.
terms.mom_warm = mommy
terms.mom_plain = mom
terms.dad_warm = daddy
terms.dad_plain = dad

mean.aggressive.1 = {name} draws their weapon: You want to settle this right now?!
mean.aggressive.2 = {name} clenches their fists: Repeat that to my face if you have the guts!
mean.aggressive.3 = {name} pushes you: Who do you think you are to talk to me like that?!
mean.aggressive.4 = {name} yells furiously: Shut up before I make you shut up!
mean.aggressive.5 = {name} spits on the ground: You'll regret opening that mouth.
mean.needy.1 = {name} almost cries: Why are you so mean to me? What did I do to you?
mean.needy.2 = {name} gets teary-eyed: I thought we were friends...
mean.needy.3 = {name} sniffs hurt: Your words really hurt, you know?
mean.needy.4 = {name} lowers their head sadly: You didn't have to be so rude... I was just here.
mean.needy.5 = {name} says with a trembling voice: I... I thought you were a better person.
mean.normal.1 = You insulted {name}! The conversation became extremely tense.
mean.normal.2 = {name} ignores you coldly, turning their back.
mean.normal.3 = {name} looks at you with disgust: You must have a very sad life to talk like that about others.
mean.normal.4 = {name} retorts with disdain: Said the role model. Look in the mirror.
mean.normal.5 = {name} answers dryly: I don't waste my time talking to your kind.
gift.loves = {name} beams: Oh my god, {itemName}?! This is my favorite! You know me so well!
gift.hates = {name} grimaces in disgust: Eww... {itemName}? I hate this! Are you trying to insult me?
gift.trash = {name} frowns angrily: {itemName}? Why are you giving me trash?!
gift.greedy = {name} widens their eyes: For me?! Haha, {itemName}! Finally someone who values me!
gift.paranoid = {name} looks at the gift ({itemName}) suspiciously: This isn't poisoned, is it?
gift.normal = {name} smiles: Wow, {itemName}! Thank you so much for the gift.
gift.basic = {name} thanks you politely: Thank you for this, it's simple but it will be useful!
gift.hobby = {name} genuinely lights up: {itemName}! How did you know? This is exactly my kind of thing.
gift.fed = {name} devours the {itemName} on the spot: Ahhh, I was starving. Thank you, really.
gift.fed_favorite = {name} snatches the {itemName} from your hand: MY FAVORITE! And I was starving! You're the best!
gift.fed_hated = {name} eats the {itemName} with a grimace: I hate this... but I'm too hungry to complain.
prof.assign.unknown = {name} looks confused at the {itemName}: ...and what do I do with this? This isn't a work tool!
prof.assign.already = {name}: I'm already a {profName}, forgot? I'm working on it every day!
prof.assign.dislike.1 = {name} makes a disgusted face: {profName}?! Not even dead! I hate that kind of work!
prof.assign.dislike.2 = {name} crosses their arms: No, thanks. {profName} is not for me. I hate it.
prof.assign.dislike.3 = {name} pushes the {itemName} back: Are you kidding? I would despise being a {profName}!
prof.assign.dislike.4 = {name} shakes their head: No way. {profName} is the last thing I want to be.
prof.assign.dislike.5 = {name} steps back: Not {profName}, please. I've suffered enough with that kind of work already.
prof.assign.dislike.6 = {name} looks at the {itemName} like it's trash: Me, a {profName}? Only in your dreams.
prof.assign.dislike.7 = {name} makes a face: That's not my thing. {profName} isn't my style.
prof.assign.dislike.8 = {name} turns away: I'd rather not even look at that. {profName} was never for me.
prof.assign.dislike.9 = {name}: No offense, but I'd rather do almost anything else before {profName}.
prof.assign.lazy.1 = {name} yawns: {profName}? That's too much work... I don't have the energy for that.
prof.assign.lazy.2 = {name} stretches: Heavy work? Me? Hahaha, good joke.
prof.assign.lazy.3 = {name} sighs: Look, thanks for the offer, but... no can do. Too much sweat involved.
prof.assign.lazy.4 = {name} pretends not to hear and stays right where they're lying in the shade.
prof.assign.lazy.5 = {name} looks at the {itemName}, then at you: That kind of work is tiring just to look at. Pass.
prof.assign.lazy.6 = {name} flops onto the ground: {profName}? That sounds tiring just to think about.
prof.assign.lazy.7 = {name} closes their eyes: We'll talk about work later. Much later.
prof.assign.lazy.8 = {name} yawns again: I was so comfortable until you showed up with that offer.
prof.assign.lazy.9 = {name}: Work today? Let me think... no.
prof.assign.aggressive.1 = {name} growls: {profName}?! Do I look like someone who plants little flowers?!
prof.assign.aggressive.2 = {name} beats their chest: I am a warrior, not a peasant! Respect me!
prof.assign.aggressive.3 = {name} spits on the ground: Too tame work for me. Give me something with action!
prof.assign.aggressive.4 = {name} looks at the {itemName} with disdain: That's work for delicate hands. Not mine.
prof.assign.aggressive.5 = {name} crosses their arms: {profName}? I want action, not tending plants or fish.
prof.assign.aggressive.6 = {name} cracks their knuckles: Manual labor? I'd rather settle things with my fists.
prof.assign.aggressive.7 = {name} looks at the {itemName} with disdain: That doesn't cut or hurt anyone. Not interested.
prof.assign.aggressive.8 = {name} stomps their foot: I was born to fight, not to plant or wash anything.
prof.assign.aggressive.9 = {name} grits their teeth: {profName} is work for weak people. I'm not weak.
prof.assign.angry.1 = {name} yells: I'M NOT IN THE MOOD FOR THIS! Come back later!
prof.assign.angry.2 = {name} looks at you angrily: Not now! I'm too pissed off to think about a job!
prof.assign.angry.3 = {name} pushes the item away: Go away! Don't come with proposals now!
prof.assign.angry.4 = {name} doesn't even look at you: Get that offer out of my sight.
prof.assign.angry.5 = {name} takes a deep, irritated breath: Not today. Not any day soon, either.
prof.assign.angry.6 = {name} completely ignores you, still fuming.
prof.assign.angry.7 = {name}: Go away. Now. This isn't the time for job talk.
prof.assign.angry.8 = {name} clenches their fists: You picked the worst possible moment for this.
prof.assign.angry.9 = {name} turns their back without a word, still visibly upset.
prof.assign.return = {name} gives you back your {profName} tools.
prof.assign.liked.1 = {name} takes the {itemName} with sparkling eyes: {profName}?! I ALWAYS wanted to do this! Thank you!
prof.assign.liked.2 = {name} almost jumps with joy: Seriously, I'm going to be a {profName}?! This is my dream!
prof.assign.liked.3 = {name} holds the {itemName} dearly: Finally someone recognizes my talent! I'll be the best {profName} ever!
prof.assign.liked.4 = {name} lets out a happy shriek: {profName}?! I would have begged if I had to! Absolutely yes!
prof.assign.liked.5 = {name} holds the {itemName} like a treasure: This has always been my dream. Thank you for trusting me with it!
prof.assign.liked.6 = {name} jumps with joy holding the {itemName}: I can't believe it! Finally, {profName}!
prof.assign.liked.7 = {name}: This is everything I've ever wanted! Thank you so much for thinking of me!
prof.assign.liked.8 = {name} hugs you out of nowhere: You have no idea how much this means to me!
prof.assign.liked.9 = {name} holds the {itemName} with both hands, emotional: {profName}... finally.
prof.assign.accept.1 = {name} takes the {itemName} and nods: Ok, {profName} sounds good. I'll do my best!
prof.assign.accept.2 = {name} examines the {itemName}: Hmm, {profName}... I can try. Thanks for the opportunity!
prof.assign.accept.3 = {name} smiles: {profName}? Sure! I'll start right now.
prof.assign.accept.4 = {name} puts away the {itemName}: Alright, I accept being a {profName}. Count on me!
prof.assign.accept.5 = {name} tests the {itemName}: I've never worked with this, but I'm excited to learn!
prof.assign.greedy.1 = {name} examines the {itemName} and frowns: {profName}?! What do I gain from this? There's no profit in that!
prof.assign.greedy.2 = {name} crosses their arms: {profName} won't fill my pockets. If there's no gold involved, forget it!
prof.assign.greedy.3 = {name} hands the item back: I only work if it's very lucrative. {profName} doesn't even pay my bills!
prof.assign.paranoid.1 = {name} backs away in fear: Working as a {profName} out there?! Do you want monsters to get me?!
prof.assign.paranoid.2 = {name} glances around suspiciously: {profName} is way too dangerous... I don't trust this at all!
prof.assign.paranoid.3 = {name} shakes their head nervously: Danger is everywhere in that job. I'm not risking my neck!
prof.assign.shy.1 = {name} blushes and hides their face: I-I... don't think I can be a {profName}... I'm too timid...
prof.assign.shy.2 = {name} steps back: That's too much responsibility for me... I'd rather stay in my corner.
prof.assign.shy.3 = {name} looks at the ground: I don't think I have what it takes to be a {profName}... I'm sorry...
prof.assign.picky.1 = {name} crosses their arms: That's not my cup of tea. I only do work that I genuinely enjoy!
prof.assign.picky.2 = {name} shakes their head: {profName}? Doesn't suit me at all. Find someone else for this.
prof.assign.picky.3 = {name} politely declines: I have no passion for {profName}. I really need to love what I do!
prof.assign.indifferent_refuse.1 = {name} shrugs: Nah, I'm not really in the mood to commit to {profName} right now.
prof.assign.indifferent_refuse.2 = {name} yawns: Maybe another day... I'm not in the headspace to start being a {profName}.
prof.assign.indifferent_refuse.3 = {name}: We aren't close enough for you to start handing me work duties.
prof.assign.easy.1 = {name} eagerly grabs the {itemName}: {profName}?! Count on me! I'll do my very best to help the village!
prof.assign.easy.2 = {name} smiles brightly: Love the idea! You can count on me as your new {profName}!
prof.assign.easy.3 = {name} gives a thumbs up: I'm in! Let's help this village thrive!
prof.assign.indifferent.1 = {name} takes the {itemName} casually: Fine by me. Work is work, as long as it helps out.
prof.assign.indifferent.2 = {name} shrugs and pockets the item: Alright. If a {profName} is needed, I can pitch in.
prof.assign.indifferent.3 = {name} nods calmly: Sure thing. I'll see what I can do as a {profName}.
cooldown.friendly = {name} waves quickly: Hi, we already talked a lot today, right?
cooldown.gift = {name}: More gifts? Oh, ok... thank you.
cooldown.general = {name} looks busy and just mutters something.
marriage.accept.1 = {name} cries with joy: Yes! A thousand times yes! I accept to marry you!
marriage.accept.2 = {name} puts on the ring with a shaking hand: I accept! I want to spend the rest of my life by your side!
marriage.reject.1 = {name}: Marriage?! I think we are moving too fast... We need to get to know each other better first.
marriage.reject.2 = {name}: I'm sorry, but I don't feel the same way about you yet...
marriage.already_married = {name}: Wait, but we are already married!
marriage.target_already_married = {name}: I'm already married to someone else... I'm sorry.
funny.cheerup.1 = {name} wipes a tear and smiles: Haha... thanks. I really needed that right now.
funny.cheerup.2 = {name}: You always know how to make me smile, even when I'm down.
funny.cheerup.3 = {name} laughs softly: Okay, that was actually pretty good.
funny.enemy.1 = {name}: Save your breath. You're not funny.
funny.enemy.2 = {name} rolls their eyes: Was that supposed to be a joke? Pathetic.
funny.enemy.3 = {name}: Do yourself a favor and stop trying to be a comedian.
romantic.stranger.1 = {name} steps back: Whoa, boundaries! We don't even know each other!
romantic.stranger.2 = {name} looks uncomfortable: That's... inappropriate for strangers.
romantic.stranger.3 = {name}: Are you always this forward with people you just met?
romantic.enemy.1 = {name} looks disgusted: Are you out of your mind? Stay away from me!
romantic.enemy.2 = {name}: I'd rather date a zombie than listen to your cheap lines.
romantic.enemy.3 = {name}: Don't even try it. I despise you.
romantic.partner.1 = {name} winks: You're still as charming as the day we met.
romantic.partner.2 = {name}: Flirting with me? You already won my heart, you know.
romantic.partner.3 = {name} pulls you closer: Keep talking like that...
romantic.partner.4 = {name}: Stop it, you're making me blush all over again!
romantic.partner.5 = {name}: I am so incredibly lucky to have you.
mean.partner.1 = {name} looks heartbroken: How could you say that to me?! I thought you loved me!
mean.partner.2 = {name} tears up: That... that really hurts coming from you.
mean.partner.3 = {name}: I don't know who you are right now. Don't speak to me.
prof.assign.refuse_status.1 = {name} scoffs: Why would I work for someone like you? No way.
prof.assign.refuse_status.2 = {name}: I don't take orders from strangers. Find someone else to be a {profName}.
prof.assign.refuse_status.3 = {name}: You must be joking. I'm not doing any {profName} work for you.
prof.assign.refuse_status.4 = {name} raises an eyebrow: And who are you to offer me work? We don't even know each other.
prof.assign.refuse_status.5 = {name} gives a dry laugh: {profName}? For you? Not even if it were the last job in Orbis.
prof.assign.refuse_status.6 = {name} doesn't even give you their attention: Work for someone I just met? Pass.
prof.assign.refuse_status.7 = {name} lets out a mocking laugh: You have to earn my respect first. This isn't a good start.
prof.assign.refuse_status.8 = {name}: I choose who I work for. And today isn't your turn.
prof.assign.refuse_status.9 = {name} crosses their arms: Prove you deserve my trust first, then we can talk about {profName}.
prof.assign.noitem = {name} looks at you confused: You're not holding anything... How am I supposed to know what job you want me to do?
prof.assign.child = {name} is just a child and cannot work yet!
armor.equip = {name} puts on the {itemName} and adjusts the straps: I'll wear this, thanks for the protection!
armor.child = {name} is just a child and shouldn't wear armour!
armor.unavailable = {name} isn't around to put this on right now.
flirt.child = You can't flirt with a child!
gift.noitem = You are not holding any item to give as a gift!
gift.accelerated.1 = {name} happily ate {item} -- that gave their growth a little push!
gift.accelerated.2 = Good call: {name} devoured {item} right away, and their growth sped up a bit.
gift.accelerated.3 = {name} thanked you with a full mouth of {item} -- growing a little faster now.
gift.child_reject.1 = {name} is just a child and doesn't want this gift. Try giving some food!
gift.child_reject.2 = {name} looks at the gift, confused -- kids don't care about that. How about some food instead?
gift.child_reject.3 = {name} shrugs: that's not for a child. Bring something to eat.
gift.baby_reject = You can't gift a baby away! Use the spouse's inventory to hand off custody instead.

# MOTHER AI
